A||N||16||trigger||bought second fiero today.  what do I do with two 88s?||||1||
Z||000000||trigger||11-24-2001||11:28 PM||||I have had my 88 coupe 4cyl auto for going on two years now and have been looking for a V-6 5spd donor for almost as long.  I picked up a Formula today and am almost tempted to just fix it.  I have to get it running first, hopefully it's nothing to big.  Other than being really dirty, needing a belt, and a wire connector for the coil everything looks ok.  The main problem is getting a title seeing as I bought it from a salvage yard.  It's the same color as my other one, bright red.  I wanted to use a bunch of parts on my coupe, but now what?  The Formula only has around 80,000 miles.  It has sunroof, rear defrost, cruise, and air.  I made a tentative list of some parts I'll probably need but I haven't even dug into it yet.  Thanks for any advice.  I'll try and get pictures.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
