Z||000006||Sootah||11-25-2001||11:51 AM||||<B>TITLE</B>: I just went through getting a title for a car like you have to.<P>Step 1: Go to the DMV and find out who currently owns the car. This may require you to send a $2 check and write a letter telling why you want the info and mailing it to your states Primary DMV place if you have the 'protected information' crap like we do here in Utah. That's what I had to do, but at least they sent the requested info back within a few days.<P>Step 2: Send a certified letter to the last owner of the vehicle requesting the title to it, not sure exactly what you would say since you bought it from a salvage yard. <P>Step 3: If the letter comes back undeliverable then just take it to the DMV <B><I>UNOPENED</B></I> along with a copy of the letter that you sent and they should give you the title. If the person does respond then you may be able to just get them to sign the car over or you may have to bribe them.<P>Since you are going through a salvage yard I don't know how much of this applies to you. It entirely possible that you could go to the DMV show them the salvage yards bill of sale and just get a salvage title. Then again, who wants a salvage title..?<P><B>PEACE <I>-Sootah</B></I><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">        <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||3
Z||000007||trigger||11-25-2001||10:05 PM||||started some clean up and work on the Formula today.  got the coil wire installed, put my battery in it, hit the key, and click.  I pulled the starter off the it is toast.  I'll get a used one off another car in my friend's grandpa's junkyard cheap and see what happen's.  tommorrow after school I'll change the oil and see if it's ok.  no coolant, no steel shavings.  I just hope the bottom end's ok.<P>smoooooth gt-  the coupe is in no way going to be a donor car.  I think the Formula is though.  The main chassis is ok, but the cradle is rusted really bad.  Somebody cut out the brake junction box.  This is the only V-6 fiero that has popped up around here for a long time.  There is one that I know of an hour away that the motor is gone, but the getrag is still there. i might go check it out.<P>thanks for the replies.  i'll have to look into a title||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever3000||11-26-2001||09:24 AM||||<B>Any</B> Fiero, but especially an 88, if it <B>can</B> be saved, <B>should</B> be saved!  If you don't have the means to fix the Formula, however, we'll understand.  I would love to put another powerplant in my 88 coupe, but it's just too nice to justify doing that.  It's worth more (to some people) in its all-stock, all-original, 2nd-owner, under-90000-miles condition.<P>Good luck, whichever way you go.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000009||Fformula88||11-26-2001||12:38 PM||||I think you should save the Formula, even if there is rust on the cradle.  If its too bad you can always swap out the cradle at some point in the future.  Its an 88 with a V6 engine, and that makes it valuable in itself.<P>Formula's in junk yards?  There was never much of a chance of finding one in a junk yard.  Not to say it doesn't happen, but the Formula is one of the most rare Fiero models produced with only 5484 made (I think thats the number, its close and since I am at work I have no way to confirm it).  Subtract the ones still operational, the ones wrecked long ago, and there just aren't too many left to head off to junk yards.<P>Here is what you do with two 88's.  Keep the 4 cyl, drive it as your daily driver.  Keep the Formula.  Start working on it to get it running and maybe do some restoration work on it.  Enjoy!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroMontreal||11-26-2001||05:05 PM||||5643 Formula's were built. If I were you I would keep this car and build it back up when you have the money. The Forumla is my fav fiero. Even if there is a bit of rust on It i am sure it's not that bad. Try to get us some picS!<BR>Thanks<BR>Alex<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
