Z||000013||Cheever3000||11-27-2001||12:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>What 88 database guy?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>He's a Forum member (88 Database Guy) who is tracking as many of them as possible.  Doing a great job of it, too.  We try to remind anybody who has any knowledge of 88 Fieros to keep him informed, especially when they change hands or go to the yard.  His email is in his profile... john.willhoff@lmco.com. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Elvira||11-27-2001||08:05 AM||||Formula's in junk yards? There was never much of a chance of finding one in a junk yard. Not to say it doesn't happen, but the Formula is one of the most rare Fiero models produced with only 5484 made (I think thats the number, its close and since I am at work I have no way to confirm it). Subtract the ones still operational, the ones wrecked long ago, and there just aren't too many left to head off to junk yards.<P>There is a maroon Formula in a junkyard in MA.  It had 40k miles on it.  The seats are now in Chester's 86GT and it is pretty much gutted out, but it IS a formula.  What a waste!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||1
